{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: moved the neural-network logits computation until after all parameter prior sampling statements so no parameter is used before its prior. Replaced `to_vector(alpha) ~ ...` and `to_vector(beta) ~ ...` with equivalent matrix-vectorized priors on the top-level parameters `alpha` and `beta`. Replaced the loop of indexed likelihood statements `y[n] ~ categorical_logit(...)` with a single vectorized built-in statement `y ~ categorical_logit(v)` using a local `array[N] vector[K]` of logits. `data_safe.json` is identical to the supplied data.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N; // observations (Full MNIST: 60K)
  int<lower=0> M; // predictors   (MNIST: 784)
  matrix[N, M] x; // data matrix  (Full MNIST: 60K x 784 = 47M)
  int<lower=2> K; // number of categories (MNIST: 10)
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> y; // categories
}
transformed data {
  int<lower=1> J = 10; // number of hidden units (e.g. 100)

  // prior parametrization in Lampinen and Vehtari (2001)
  real nu_alpha = 0.5;
  real s2_0_alpha = (0.05 / M ^ (1 / nu_alpha)) ^ 2;
  real nu_beta = 0.5;
  real s2_0_beta = (0.05 / J ^ (1 / nu_beta)) ^ 2;

  vector[N] ones = rep_vector(1, N);
  matrix[N, M + 1] x1 = append_col(ones, x);
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma2_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma2_beta;
  matrix[M, J] alpha;
  matrix[J, K - 1] beta;
  row_vector[J] alpha1;
  row_vector[K - 1] beta1;
}
model {
  // Priors
  alpha1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma2_alpha ~ inv_gamma(nu_alpha / 2, nu_alpha * s2_0_alpha / 2);
  sigma2_beta ~ inv_gamma(nu_beta / 2, nu_beta * s2_0_beta / 2);

  alpha ~ normal(0, sqrt(sigma2_alpha));
  beta ~ normal(0, sqrt(sigma2_beta));

  {
    matrix[N, K] v_matrix;
    array[N] vector[K] v;
    v_matrix = append_col(ones,
                          append_col(ones,
                                     tanh(x1 * append_row(alpha1, alpha)))
                          * append_row(beta1, beta));
    for (n in 1 : N) {
      v[n] = v_matrix[n]';
    }
    y ~ categorical_logit(v);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":2,"M":3,"N":2,"x":[[6.380649506540683,3.223614298877222,4.593196136567718],[2.3606350985893862,5.055995227424176,3.1817588756124096]],"y":[2,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
